cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DocMut, please cite it."
title: "DocMut: Deterministic Multi-Format Document Mutation for LaTeX, Typst, and Markdown"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-02"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Venkateshmurthy
    given-names: Prajwal S.
repository-code: "https://github.com/prajwal-svm/docmut"
url: "https://github.com/prajwal-svm/docmut"
keywords:
  - mutation testing
  - LaTeX
  - Typst
  - Markdown
  - document repair
  - benchmark construction
  - synthetic faults
  - engine-gated evaluation
abstract: >-
  DocMut is a deterministic, multi-format document mutation library for
  constructing engine-validated synthetic faults in LaTeX, Typst, and Markdown.
  It targets scholarly document structure, separates hard compile failures from
  soft diagnostic faults, retains mutants under a pinned compilation gate, and
  optionally drops render-text-equivalent mutants via PDF text comparison. It
  uses a surface structural parse adequate for site selection, not a full TeX
  expansion engine, and does not claim natural error prevalence or complete
  semantic equivalence detection.
